Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and potential usage  
• "collection_name": filter rows belonging to the wanted collection (‘qin_prostate_repeatability’) in IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL.  
• "SeriesDescription": free‑text description of each MR series; look for substrings such as ‘T2’, ‘AXIAL’, ‘T2W’, etc.  
• "Modality": modality code; restrict to 'MR'.  
• "StudyInstanceUID": study‑level identifier; used to assemble the final list and to join with the SEGMENTATIONS table.  
• "SegmentedPropertyType": VARIANT with keys such as "CodeMeaning"; search for CodeMeaning ILIKE '%peripheral%zone%' to find the desired anatomic structure.  
• SEGMENTATIONS."StudyInstanceUID": lets you map segmentation‑level records to the imaging studies collected from DICOM_ALL.  

Typical conditions that may be applied  
• DICOM_ALL."collection_name" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'  
• DICOM_ALL."Modality" = 'MR'  
• DICOM_ALL."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%' AND DICOM_ALL."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%AXIAL%'  
• SEGMENTATIONS."SegmentedPropertyType":"CodeMeaning"::STRING ILIKE '%peripheral%zone%'  

Below are 10 exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progress from simple inspection to the combined logic needed for the task.  

```sql
-- 1) Check that the collection name exists and see a few rows
SELECT DISTINCT "collection_name"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE "collection_name" ILIKE '%qin%prostate%repeatability%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) List MR series descriptions in the collection to verify naming conventions
SELECT DISTINCT "SeriesDescription"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE "collection_name" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND "Modality" = 'MR'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Find series descriptions containing the word T2
SELECT DISTINCT "SeriesDescription"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE "collection_name" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND "Modality" = 'MR'
  AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Find series descriptions that look axial as well
SELECT DISTINCT "SeriesDescription"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE "collection_name" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND "Modality" = 'MR'
  AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%'
  AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%AXIAL%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Grab studies (UIDs) that contain at least one T2‑weighted axial MR series
SELECT DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE "collection_name" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND "Modality" = 'MR'
  AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%'
  AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%AXIAL%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Peek at how the segmentation “SegmentedPropertyType” JSON looks
SELECT "SegmentedPropertyType"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS"
WHERE "SegmentedPropertyType" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Extract the CodeMeaning element to see possible values
SELECT DISTINCT
       "SegmentedPropertyType":"CodeMeaning"::STRING AS "CodeMeaning"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS"
WHERE "SegmentedPropertyType" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) List studies that have segmentation CodeMeaning containing 'Peripheral zone'
SELECT DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS"
WHERE LOWER("SegmentedPropertyType":"CodeMeaning"::STRING) ILIKE '%peripheral%zone%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Combine steps 5 and 8 with an inner join to verify overlap
SELECT DISTINCT t2."StudyInstanceUID"
FROM (
      SELECT DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID"
      FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
      WHERE "collection_name" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
        AND "Modality" = 'MR'
        AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%'
        AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%AXIAL%'
     ) AS t2
JOIN (
      SELECT DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID"
      FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS"
      WHERE LOWER("SegmentedPropertyType":"CodeMeaning"::STRING) ILIKE '%peripheral%zone%'
     ) AS seg
  ON t2."StudyInstanceUID" = seg."StudyInstanceUID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final distinct StudyInstanceUIDs meeting both criteria (full answer list, still limited here)
SELECT DISTINCT t2."StudyInstanceUID"
FROM (
      SELECT DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID"
      FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
      WHERE "collection_name" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
        AND "Modality" = 'MR'
        AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%'
        AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%AXIAL%'
     ) AS t2
INNER JOIN "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS" seg
        ON t2."StudyInstanceUID" = seg."StudyInstanceUID"
WHERE LOWER(seg."SegmentedPropertyType":"CodeMeaning"::STRING) ILIKE '%peripheral%zone%'
LIMIT 20;
```
